rd practice across  the entire state  so you know unfortunately the smaller  police department sometimes are slow to  move or they need help from a larger  police department because of resources  availability  and they use the the policies and  procedures and the language  associated with how we conduct business  from a big department onto their  department and  it's it's i'm actually pretty proud of  what i'm seeing up there  because they're taking what we've  seen and what we've adjusted for and  what we're putting into place  into place across the state and then in  turn you're seeing similar actions  across the united states with all police  departments let's switch gears a little  bit  sheriff you recently went public with  the las vegas review journal about your  potential plans to change jobs and  potentially run for governor  where do things stand right now for the  possible run for another office in 2022  well i appreciate the question but i'm  still in the same situation as i  described to the review journal  you know my primary focus right now is  being your clark county sheriff  that's what i was voted in for  to do but yeah but you know you look at  new challenges in life and you  and you figure out what you're going to  do into the future  and maybe you can affect some larger  changes in another  position and i will make a decision on  that here in  in the very short future more than  likely in the next few weeks on what i'm  planning on doing for the state of  nevada  what is it about the current  administration that maybe would motivate  you to consider running for governor  i just think we can do it better and  that would be  the line i would use can you be more  specific about doing it better  no i'm worried about my job as a sheriff  right now  all right just a brief response there  from sheriff lombardo meanwhile a  potential republican field for governor  slowly taking shape north las vegas  mayor john lee recently switched to the  republican party  and this week he announced a 17 county  all the counties  nevada campaign swing starting in  esmeralda county now  lee has not officially announced he's  running for governor yet but this might  be  first salvo well this week we're  bringing back our  following the money segment and first  quarter fundraising totals are in we're  focusing on a couple of nevada's key  races for 2022.  as you see behind me there democratic  senator catherine cortez masto raised  2.3  million dollars in the first quarter she  has about 4.7 million dollars  in cash on hand as for democratic  congresswoman suzy lee she raised about  607  thousand dollars for her district 3 race  as you can see  she has 484 thousand dollars of cash  on hand and congressman stephen horsford  raised 363 000  he is in of course congressional  district four and he has seven hundred  fifty seven thousand dollars in cash on  hand  no major republican challengers have  taken shape yet  you're watching politics now  finally here on politics now florida  governor ron desantis is going to be at  the basque fry fundraiser held by adam  laxalt every year here in nevada  the republican event is going to be  august 14th in gardnerville  no other speakers have been announced  yet but in the past it's been aligned  with cpac  former vice president mike pence among  others have spoken there before  we'll see you next week here on politics  now thanks for watching
 

